{
  "abstract": "For a metric continuum X, D(X) is the hyperspace of subcontinua of X that are the closure of their interior, with the Hausdorff metric. The project formalizes the theorem that a countable D(X) is a G-delta subset of the hyperspace of subcontinua, hence completely metrizable and scattered with dense isolated points, so that D(X) is never homeomorphic to the rationals; together with the structure theory behind it (independent families, blister theorem, complement lemma, absorption by minimal elements, decreasing intersections, density of minimal elements, D-atomic continua, the cardinality dichotomy).",
  "authors": [
    {
      "name": "Lucas Alves de Almeida"
    }
  ],
